  <!-- plone.pageletlayout is an INTEGRATION package (templates + chrome
       pagelets), NOT a theme: under the two-package re-role (wayfinder ticket
       04) it ships NO theme CSS, and under wayfinder ticket 15 it ships NO CSS
       AT ALL. It registers ZERO bundles.

       The whole layered cascade — the @layer declaration, Bootstrap, the
       plone-prefixed custom-property tokens, primitives, the bs-to-plone bridge,
       and the component hooks — lives in plonetheme.clara's single compiled
       bundle (theme/scss/clara.scss builds clara.min.css). The six former theme
       bundles (pageletlayout-layers, bootstrap5, pageletlayout-tokens,
       pageletlayout-primitives, pageletlayout-bridge, pageletlayout-components)
       left in ticket 04.

       The last CSS the base still shipped — pageletlayout-toolbar, the editor
       chrome — left in ticket 15: toolbar styling is theme-owned (exactly as
       stock Plone ships barceloneta-toolbar.min.css inside the Barceloneta
       *theme*), so its #edit-zone chrome moved into clara.min.css and the base
       became literally zero-CSS. Any non-Clara consumer (e.g. the eventual
       plone.app.layout upstream home) ships the editor toolbar unstyled unless
       it provides its own theme.

       upgrades.py purges every relocated bundle record from already-installed
       sites (step 1000→1001: the six theme bundles; 1001→1002: the toolbar). -->

</registry>
